{"tool_name":"gatk_pathseq","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"GATK_PathSeq","home":"https://github.com/broadinstitute/gatk","license":"BSD-3-Clause","summary":"Customizable computational tool included in Genome Analysis Toolkit (GATK) for the discovery and identification of microbial sequences in libraries from eukaryotic hosts.","addition_date":"2019-07-06T07:21:21Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:07:41.085500Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:GATK_PathSeq","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"matthew_meyerson@dfci.harvard.edu","name":"Matthew Meyerson","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/broadinstitute/gatk/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence trimming","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3192"}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"GATK PathSeq","operating_system":["Linux","Mac"],"owner":"Ruta","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/bty501","metadata":{"abstract":"We present an updated version of our computational pipeline, PathSeq, for the discovery and identification of microbial sequences in genomic and transcriptomic libraries from eukaryotic hosts. This pipeline is available in the Genome Analysis Toolkit (GATK) as a suite of configurable tools that can report the microbial composition of DNA or RNA short-read sequencing samples and identify unknown sequences for downstream assembly of novel organisms. GATK PathSeq enables sample analysis in minutes at low cost. In addition, these tools are built with the GATK engine and Apache Spark framework, providing robust, rapid parallelization of read quality filtering, host subtraction and microbial alignment in workstation, cluster and cloud environments.","authors":[{"name":"Bullman S."},{"name":"Meyerson M."},{"name":"Ojesina A.I."},{"name":"Pedam